\section{Conclusion}
In this work, we propose cost functions with a corresponding weight learning method that allows for efficient optimization of either MI or BMI using standard automatic differentiation coupled with gradient ascent. We show analytically that our new approach also uses exact gradients of the constellation point probabilities for the optimization as in~\cite{Aref22}. The simulation results of the proposed weight learning method closely match the results from the method in~\cite{Aref22} for the AWGN channel and a simplified model of the optical IM/DD channel. The proposed cost functions are easier to implement as they do not require the manual computation of additional gradient terms and are also applicable to other channel models.
