\noindent Partial orders are closed under concatenation of local chains, so while this construction is a strict subset, it guarantees the property holds. $M^{X}$ with disjoint block structure guarantees $\mathbb{Z}$-linear eigenvalues and provides users with a simple and well-leveraged interface, while pre-computing the direct filtration increases speed \& scalability. 

