\noindent Users provide a small number of degrees of freedom in a highly flexible subset of $M^X$. Such matrices are desirable for Markov-type systems which are non-dissipative but not necessarily reversible (fig. \ref{fig:oo}). For users who want to avoid dealing with the complex relationships between the partial order and its corresponding matrix, or prefer to use matrix dimension as input, the stochastic subset from local disjoint transposition chains will be of interest.
