\section*{Future Directions}
A similar treatment for eigenvectors is equally important. Generating a closest suitable matrix still requires expert knowledge for distance norm selection and usage, so a procedural method for inferring $\mathbb{Z}$-linear matrices would be useful. Developed understanding of real-coefficient constructions is needed.  We suspect that more efficient encodings could decrease the required number of batches.  We look forward to progress in computing fast eigenvalues with complex algebraic structure through novel means of encoding symbolic terms in a numeric context.

