\section{Related Work}
\label{sec:related}
%

%
Generating synthetic data with DP has an extensive literature, particularly over categorical features~\cite{BLR08,HR10,DNR09,VAA22,HRZ24}. Many such approaches rely on the exponential mechanism~\cite{hardt2012simple,AL23,PGM23}. Unfortunately, it is cryptographically hard to generate DP synthetic data that preserves all 2-way marginals with polynomial sample complexity~\cite{UV11}; see also~\cite[Thm. 6.12]{Va17} and~\cite[Ch. 9]{dwork2014dp}. However, the advent of generative AI pretrained on web-scale data provides strong priors over data distributions, allowing a partial circumvention of these lower bounds. This led to a flurry of recent work to generate complex image/text data with DP~\cite{dpanon,dpdm,privimage,VCH+22,API1,xie2024dpsyndata}. We focus on practical and scalable DP text generation.

%
DP text can be generated as a post-processing of DP fine-tuned models~\cite{AMR+19,MJW+22,yue2023syntextgen,kurakin2024llm,yu2024dpinstruct} or via private inference.\footnote{
    Private inference can be used on pretrained models prompted with private data (our setting) or non-DP fine-tuned models. Both are conceptually identical as they privatize a set of non-private predictions.
}
We focus on the latter as the private fine-tuning can be prohibitively expensive, especially with large models~\cite{ponomareva2023dp}. Private inference can be further divided based on the type of access to the LLM: via a token/text generation API~\cite{wu2023dpicl,xie2024dpsyndata,yu2024dpinstruct}, or through white-box access to model internals such as next-token logits~\cite{wu2023dpicl,tang2024privateicl,amin2024private}; we focus on the white-box setting.
Other DP text manipulation tasks include paraphrasing~\cite{CVF21,UHC23} and next-token prediction~\cite{MDP+22,ginart2022submix,flemings2024pmixed,flemings2024adapmixed}. (We adapt \cite{flemings2024adapmixed} to text generation as a baseline in our empirical comparisons.)


%
Most prior approaches to DP text generation suffer from one or more restrictions:
(1) a small number of generations, enough to serve as exemplars for in-context learning~\cite{duan2023stochparrots,tang2024privateicl,hong2024dpopt};
(2) short or highly constrained generations in classification or directed text generation tasks such as summarization or question-answering (as opposed to open-ended long-form generation)~\cite{wu2023dpicl,amin2024private}.
Of these, only the API-access method of \cite{xie2024dpsyndata} and the white-box method of \cite{amin2024private, amin2025private} apply to long-form generation. 

The concurrent work of \cite{amin2025private} extends the approach of \citet{amin2024private} by clustering similar references into a batch. This orthogonal approach can also be integrated with \method for synthetic text generation, though we note that clustering may not be applicable to some DP text generation tasks, such as RAG. Additionally, \cite{amin2025private} replaces mean aggregation of (clipped) logits with median aggregation, which has a smaller local sensitivity and results in a tighter \emph{ex-post} DP guarantee \cite{ligett2017expost}, i.e.,  the DP guarantee is evaluated after the algorithm’s output is observed. In contrast, \method provides a stronger standard (\emph{ex-ante}) DP guarantee, which can be evaluated before the algorithm is run. Similar to \citet{amin2024private}, the DP guarantee in \citep{amin2025private} is also data-dependent and shares the same limitations (highlighted at the end of \S\ref{sec:intro}).

%
%
%
%
%


%
Prior DP text generation approaches diverge significantly from successful decoding algorithms in the NLP literature. Indeed, sampling from truncated next-token distributions~\cite{fan2018heirarchical,holtazman2020curious,meister2022locally,hewitt2022truncation,ZHH24,MBN+25} is strongly backed by qualitative~\cite{holtazman2020curious}, quantitative~\cite{pillutla2021mauvenips,pillutla2023mauvejmlr}, and theoretical~\cite{FHK+24} evidence; see the survey~\cite{welleck2024decoding} for further details.
\method aims to generate high-utility text by adapting truncated non-private decoding to the DP setting.

