% but packing \cite{b10,b2} and preselection \cite{b11,b7,b3} are still facing three primary challenges, one for packing and two for preselection. For packing, existing schemes necessitate the collection of multiple faces prior to encryption, thereby introducing latency. For preselection, it must ensure both the security and accuracy of face recognition to prevent the omission of the target face from the candidate queue. Also, uneven distribution within a candidate queue can lead to unnecessarily large size of queue, thereby increasing computational overhead.
