\section{Enumerating Minimal Absent Subsequences Optimally}\label{sec:SASMAS2}

Firstly, we show that the strategy used to enumerate $\sas(w)$ can be used to enumerate $\mas(w)$, and obtain a result similar to, but not as efficient as, Theorem \ref{thm:SAS_enumeration}.

\begin{restatable}{theorem}{masskeletontheorem}\label{thm:MAS_skeleton}
    For a string $w\in \Sigma^n$, over an alphabet of size $\sigma$, we can construct in $\O(n\sigma)$ time an $(n+1)$-skeleton DAG $G$, with $\O(n\sigma)$ nodes, source $s$, sink $f$, such that $\mas(w)$ can be bijectively mapped to the set of $s-f$-paths of $D(G)$.
\end{restatable}
