On most small examples in \Cref{tbl:bench}, we achieve a comparable
timing with \msolve, with the exception of PS(2,12). On the larger
example RD(5) we have a small improvement, while on ED(3,3) we achieve
a much better timing. We should mention that our implementation is not
yet optimized (for example, we observed that the linear systems to be
solved in \Cref{alg:lift} are very sparse, yet our implementation
relies on dense representations and arithmetic) and does not
incorporate the idea mentioned in \Cref{rem:tracer}.

